Facility Failure Domain Registry is part of the Data Center Control Plane
(DCCP). It is DCCP boundary 49 and owns the canonical authority for physical
facility failure domains: stable failure-domain identities, typed domain
classes, membership of opaque external resource identities, nesting and overlap
relationships, shared-fate relationships, inter-domain dependency edges,
declared independence, lifecycle, provenance, generation-bound immutable
snapshots, conflict preservation and stale-generation rejection. It is built
from the C++20 standard library only.

Third-party notices
-------------------

This product includes no third-party source code and links no third-party
libraries. It is implemented against the C++20 standard library and the
operating-system interfaces it needs for durable atomic file replacement,
exclusive file locking and non-interactive process termination in tests.

The canonical serialization format, the integrity digest (SHA-256, FIPS 180-4)
and every identity, generation, epoch and incarnation type are implemented in
this repository. No third-party cryptographic library is used.

Facility Failure Domain Registry does not collect or transmit any telemetry. All
state, evidence and logs are written to local files chosen by the operator and
never leave the machine running the software.

